//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// MONEY LINE MASTER v62
//
// WHAT IT IS
//   An ATR trailing-stop regime line. Above it = bullish, below = bearish.
//   The line follows whatever timeframe the chart is on. Everything else in
//   this script qualifies that one fact — none of it changes the signal.
//
// WHAT IT WILL NOT DO
//   It does not predict. It reports which side of a line price closed on,
//   after the close. On large-cap compounders it has historically given back
//   most of the upside versus simply holding (see the HOLD vs TRADE row and
//   the three return figures). Its value there is the exit, not the entry.
//
// THE ROWS THAT MATTER MOST
//   RISK & SIZE     how far the exit sits and what position that allows
//   HOLD vs TRADE   signals vs core-200w vs buy&hold, from your start year
//   WHIPSAW         exits that bought back higher, and what they cost
//   CORE EXIT       the slow 200-bar line for a held position
//   CONFIRM         n/9 checks, direction-aware
//
// WARNINGS BUILT IN
//   ⚠ UNCONFIRMED    the bar has not closed; this can still un-happen
//   ⚠ ONLY nnd       the symbol is too young for the line to mean anything
//   ⚠ MIXED DATES    focus list symbols are reading different bars — do not act
//   ⧗ / ⚡           row is stale / crossing live but unconfirmed
//
// OUTLOOK ROW (v57)
//   Adds five votes: the money line, daily+weekly agreement, price vs the
//   auto trendlines, RSI vs 50, MACD vs its signal. It describes how much the
//   evidence AGREES right now. It is a state read, not a forecast, and it does
//   not change any signal, stat or return figure.
//
// PRO LINES (v58; v61 fixes the loop-step runtime error)
//   The long lines traders post on charts. The script tests every pair of
//   major swing highs (and swing lows), keeps only lines that price has NOT
//   closed through, and draws the one that price has respected the most
//   (touches, then length). Plus a parallel channel line and the nearest
//   horizontal level where price reacted repeatedly. Lines are drawn from
//   CLOSED bars only and re-fit when a new major swing confirms.
//
// HARD LIMIT
//   40 request.*() calls, and it uses all 40. Any new symbol, timeframe or
//   fundamental breaks the whole script silently. Reuse existing data instead.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// calc_bars_count PINS THE CALCULATION WINDOW. This is the fix for "the line
// moves when I scroll or zoom out", and it is not cosmetic.
//
// The flip rule is RECURSIVE: today's level is built from yesterday's, all the
// way back to whatever bar the calculation happened to start on. TradingView
// loads history lazily, so scrolling left or zooming out hands the script MORE
// bars, the recursion starts somewhere new, and EVERY level shifts underneath
// price. Nothing about the market changed; the starting point did.
//
// Every request.security() below already passed calc_bars_count = scanBars, so
// the Focus List was always immune. The chart's own line was the one place the
// guard was missing - which is also why the panel and the Focus List row for
// the SAME symbol could legitimately disagree. Both are pinned to 750 now.
//
// KEEP THIS EQUAL TO the "History window per symbol" input (scanBars, default
// 750) or the chart and the Focus List go back to disagreeing.
//
// COST, stated plainly: only the last 750 bars are calculated. On weekly that
// is about 14 years, so the oldest BUY/SELL labels stop being drawn and a
// "from 2010" backtest window effectively starts nearer 2012. Raise it for a
// deeper record, lower it for a lighter script.
indicator("Money Line MASTER v64", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_bars_back = 2000, calc_bars_count = 750)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE SYNTHESIS (from everything we tested):
//  • Engine = CLEAN baseline (1-close flip) → trades EVERY asset,
//    no lockouts (the ULTIMATE gates locked out TSLA & TCS)
//  • The gates (daily confluence, 200d MA, MA stack, volume, RSI)
//    now GRADE each BUY (A/B/C) instead of blocking it
//    → you never miss a trend, but you know its quality → size accordingly
//  • Long-Term row = plain-language market health for hold decisions
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── 1. Line Settings (the validated baseline) ──
longLen   = input.int(5, "Long (Bullish) Lookback", minval = 1, group = "1. Line Settings")
shortLen  = input.int(3, "Short (Bearish) Lookback", minval = 1, group = "1. Line Settings")
atrLen    = input.int(21, "ATR Length", minval = 1, group = "1. Line Settings")
atrMultL  = input.float(3.0, "ATR Multiplier — LONG stop", minval = 0.1, step = 0.05, group = "1. Line Settings")
atrMultS  = input.float(3.0, "ATR Multiplier — SHORT stop", minval = 0.1, step = 0.05, group = "1. Line Settings")
exitConfirm  = input.int(1, "Bar closes needed to SELL (chart TF)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, tooltip = "1 = sell on the FIRST weekly close below the line (original behaviour). 2 = the break must hold for two weekly closes before it counts. Higher numbers kill whipsaws but give back more before you exit. Try 2 on assets where the HOLD vs TRADE row says HOLD.", group = "1. Line Settings")
entryConfirm = input.int(1, "Bar closes needed to BUY (chart TF)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, tooltip = "Same idea for entries. 1 = original.", group = "1. Line Settings")
btUseStart = input.bool(true, "Limit stats to a start year", tooltip = "OFF = measure from the first bar TradingView loads, which is 1891 on GOLD and 1986 on MSFT. That makes Track Record, ASSET FIT and the return figures non-comparable between symbols, and on GOLD it includes the decades when the price was pegged by law. ON = every stat below is measured from your chosen year.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
btStartY   = input.int(2010, "Start year for all stats", minval = 1900, maxval = 2100, group = "4. Backtest Window")
whipWeeks  = input.int(6, "Whipsaw = re-bought within N bars", minval = 1, maxval = 26, tooltip = "An exit that is followed by a BUY within N bars AT A HIGHER PRICE is counted as a whipsaw: you sold and paid up to get back in. The row at the bottom of the table counts them and totals what they cost.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
adxMin = input.int(20, "Min ADX for a 'trending' check", minval = 10, maxval = 40, tooltip = "ADX measures how strongly price is trending, in either direction. Below this the market is ranging — the condition that produces whipsaw. 20 is the conventional threshold.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
extMax = input.float(25.0, "Max % from the 200-day-equivalent mean", minval = 5, maxval = 100, step = 1, tooltip = "Beyond this distance from the long mean, a trend is stretched and mean-reversion risk rises. The check fails above it.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
minHistDays = input.int(365, "Minimum symbol history (days) before trusting signals", minval = 30, maxval = 2000, tooltip = "Below this, the panel warns that the symbol has not existed long enough for a trailing stop to mean anything. Measured in calendar days, not bars — a newly listed stock produces plenty of 4H bars while still being only weeks old.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
riskPct = input.float(1.0, "Account risk per trade %", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10, step = 0.1, tooltip = "How much of the account you are willing to lose if the trade goes straight from here to the flip line. The RISK & SIZE row turns this into a position size. A fresh signal with a tight stop allows a big position; the same signal after price has run far from the line allows a small one.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
regimeMode = input.bool(false, "Regime mode — state, not orders", tooltip = "OFF = BUY/SELL labels and instructions, as now. ON = the chart just says what the state IS: green above the flip line, red below, with small bullish/bearish tags at the turns and no order language anywhere. IMPORTANT: this changes nothing in the maths. Trend, focus list, stats and returns are byte-identical either way. It changes what you are shown, not what the system does.", group = "5. Display Mode")

scoutPct = input.float(0.80, "Scout entry: allowed while bearish confirmation <=", minval = 0.3, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, tooltip = "Share of the applicable confirmation checks. While bearish, a daily turn-up counts as a 'scout' entry only if the downtrend is NOT confirmed above this level. The old rule was <=4 of 5, which is about 0.80.", group = "4. Backtest Window")
minTrades = input.int(12, "Min completed trades before ASSET FIT / WHIPSAW / HOLD-vs-TRADE are shown", minval = 3, maxval = 50, tooltip = "5 trades is noise. Raise this for a stricter read.", group = "4. Backtest Window")

minWin = input.float(35.0, "ASSET FIT: min win rate % (trend systems win < 50% by design)", minval = 10, maxval = 70, step = 1, tooltip = "ASSET FIT needs profit factor >= 1.5 AND a win rate above this. The old hard-coded 45 mislabelled normal trend-following results as MIXED.", group = "4. Backtest Window")

sigMax     = input.int(12, "Show only the last N BUY/SELL labels (0 = all)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, tooltip = "Zoomed out on a daily chart the labels stack into a red wall. 12 keeps the picture readable. 0 draws every signal.", group = "2. Display")
sigSizeIn  = input.string("Small", "BUY/SELL label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = "2. Display")

showPro    = input.bool(true, "PRO LINES: long trendlines + channel + key levels", tooltip = "The long clean lines: best-fit falling/rising trendline through major swings, a parallel channel line, and the nearest horizontal level where price reacted several times.", group = "2. Display")
proS       = input.int(10, "Pro lines: swing size (bars each side)", minval = 3, maxval = 40, tooltip = "Bigger = only major swings, fewer and longer lines. Smaller = tighter lines. Try 6 for a closer view, 16 for the big picture.", group = "2. Display")
proLB      = input.int(500, "Pro lines: look-back (bars)", minval = 100, maxval = 1500, group = "2. Display")
proTol     = input.float(0.6, "Pro lines: tolerance %", minval = 0.1, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.1, tooltip = "How far a close may poke through a line before the line is rejected, and how close a swing must be to count as a touch.", group = "2. Display")
showChan   = input.bool(true, "Pro lines: parallel channel line", group = "2. Display")
showKeyLv  = input.bool(true, "Pro lines: key horizontal levels", group = "2. Display")
proColor   = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 0), "Pro lines: trendline colour", group = "2. Display")
proLvlColor = input.color(color.new(#ffb300, 0), "Pro lines: key level colour", group = "2. Display")

showVL    = input.bool(true, "Vertical line at each BUY / SELL signal", tooltip = "A thin vertical line on the exact bar of each signal (same last-N cap as the labels).", group = "2. Display")
showTLV   = input.bool(true, "Vertical line at each short-trendline break (TL)", tooltip = "Blue = broke above a falling line, orange = broke below a rising line. Keeps the last 10.", group = "2. Display")
showProV  = input.bool(true, "Vertical line + label when price closes through a long trendline", tooltip = "Marks the exact bar where price closed above the long resistance line (green) or below the long support line (red).", group = "2. Display")
proRecent = input.int(15, "Pro lines: keep a broken line visible for N bars", minval = 3, maxval = 60, tooltip = "A long line is normally dropped once price closes through it. This keeps it on the chart, with its breakout marker, for N bars after the break.", group = "2. Display")

// ── 2. Display ──
bullColor = input.color(color.new(#00e676, 0), "Bullish Color", group = "2. Display")
bearColor = input.color(color.new(#ff1744, 0), "Bearish Color", group = "2. Display")
lineWidth = input.int(3, "Line Width", minval = 1, maxval = 6, group = "2. Display")
showFill  = input.bool(true, "Fill Between Price and Line", group = "2. Display")
show200   = input.bool(true, "Show 200-day MA (red)", group = "2. Display")
show200bar = input.bool(true, "Show 200-bar MA (thick black — the slow CORE line)", group = "2. Display")
ma200barLen = input.int(200, "200-bar MA Length", minval = 10, group = "2. Display")
show50bar  = input.bool(true, "Show 50-bar MA (orange)", group = "2. Display")
ma50barLen = input.int(50, "50-bar MA Length", minval = 5, group = "2. Display")
show100bar = input.bool(true, "Show 100-bar MA (blue)", group = "2. Display")
ma100barLen = input.int(100, "100-bar MA Length", minval = 5, group = "2. Display")
tablePos  = input.string("Middle Left", "Table Position", options = ["Middle Left", "Top Left", "Top Right", "Bottom Left", "Bottom Right"], group = "2. Display")
tableSize = input.string("Small", "Table Text Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = "2. Display")
compactMode = input.bool(true, "Compact Mode (3-row table + smart note; untick for full 12-row detail)", group = "2. Display")

// ── 3. Scanner (bottom-right trend overview) ──
showScanner = input.bool(true, "Show Focus List (bottom right)", group = "3. Focus List")
scanUseChart = input.bool(false, "Focus List follows the chart timeframe", tooltip = "ON = the scan runs on whatever timeframe you are viewing, so switching chart TF switches the whole list with it. OFF = the list stays pinned to the timeframe below no matter what the chart shows.", group = "3. Focus List")
scanTFin     = input.timeframe("W", "Focus List Timeframe (when not following)", group = "3. Focus List")
scanTF       = scanUseChart ? timeframe.period : scanTFin
scanPos     = input.string("Bottom Right", "Focus List Position", options = ["Bottom Right", "Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Left"], group = "3. Focus List")
maxShow     = input.int(20, "Max rows to display (most urgent first)", minval = 3, maxval = 32, group = "3. Focus List")
scanConfirmed = input.bool(true, "Confirmed bars only (identical on every chart)", tooltip = "ON = each symbol is read at its own last CLOSED weekly bar. This is what makes the Focus List give the same answer whether you are on an NSE chart or a NASDAQ chart. OFF = live/forming bar, which drifts between charts because sessions and holidays differ.", group = "3. Focus List")
scanBars      = input.int(750, "History window per symbol (bars)", minval = 100, maxval = 2000, tooltip = "Fixes how many bars each symbol is calculated over so the trailing-stop state cannot depend on how much history your current chart happens to have loaded. Keep this the same on every chart.", group = "3. Focus List")
scanNoFx      = input.bool(true, "Ignore chart currency conversion", tooltip = "Stops an INR chart from converting USD symbols (and vice versa).", group = "3. Focus List")
addChartSym   = input.bool(true, "Always scan the chart's own symbol", tooltip = "Puts whatever symbol you have open into slot 32, so a chart that is not in the market set still gets a scanner row. Turn off to keep the fixed 32nd symbol instead.", group = "3. Focus List")
mktFilter     = input.bool(false, "Show only symbols from the chart's market", tooltip = "ON = an NSE chart lists only NSE/BSE symbols, a US chart only US symbols, and so on. This removes the one-bar offset that appears when a symbol's exchange closes later than the chart's, which is the honest fix for it. Symbols entered without an exchange prefix always show. OFF = all 32 symbols, with the offset present on cross-market rows.", group = "3. Focus List")
tolBars       = input.float(1.5, "Stale threshold (bars)", minval = 1.0, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.5, tooltip = "How far behind the newest symbol a row may read before it is flagged ⧗. Measured in scan bars, not days. 1.5 is the sensible floor for a mixed-exchange list: symbols on a later-closing exchange always report one bar behind on a chart whose session ended earlier, which is correct behaviour. Raise it if the warning fires constantly; lower it toward 1.0 only on a single-exchange list.", group = "3. Focus List")
scanWarm      = input.int(120, "Warm-up bars before a symbol is trusted", minval = 40, maxval = 400, tooltip = "The trailing stop is path-dependent: it starts from an arbitrary seed and needs bars to forget it. Below this many bars a symbol's state is still partly an artefact of where its data began, so it is shown as 'warming up' rather than given a signal. Raise it if levels shift when you zoom; lower it if too many symbols are suppressed.", group = "3. Focus List")
showAsOf      = input.bool(true, "Show 'as of' date in Focus List header", tooltip = "Diagnostic: if two charts show the same as-of date, they are reading the same week.", group = "3. Focus List")
// ── MARKET BUCKETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Symbols only share a bar boundary if their sessions END together. NSE closes
// 10:00 UTC Friday, NASDAQ 20:00 UTC — so on an NSE chart every US symbol
// legitimately reports one bar behind. Filtering to the chart's own market
// removes that offset instead of tolerating it.
f_exch(_s) =>
    _i = str.pos(_s, ":")
    na(_i) ? "" : str.upper(str.substring(_s, 0, _i))

f_mkt(_p) =>
    _u = str.upper(_p)
    _u == "" ? "ANY" : _u == "NSE" or _u == "BSE" ? "IN" : _u == "NASDAQ" or _u == "NYSE" or _u == "AMEX" or _u == "ARCA" or _u == "NYSEARCA" or _u == "BATS" or _u == "CBOE" ? "US" : _u == "BINANCE" or _u == "COINBASE" or _u == "BITSTAMP" or _u == "KRAKEN" or _u == "BYBIT" ? "CRYPTO" : "OTHER"

// Exchange-string matching turned out to be unreliable — an NSE:TCS chart
// resolved to "OTHER", so the scanner fell back to the US set. Currency and
// instrument type are unambiguous and need no lookup table:
//   crypto  -> syminfo.type is "crypto" regardless of venue
//   India   -> quoted in INR
//   else    -> treated as US / global
chartMkt = syminfo.type == "crypto" ? "CRYPTO" : str.upper(syminfo.currency) == "INR" ? "IN" : "US"

// ── PER-MARKET SYMBOL SETS ───────────────────────────────────────────
// These are CONSTANTS, not inputs. 96 input.symbol() pickers pushed the script
// to 143 inputs, which appears to exceed what TradingView allows — the script
// compiled but drew nothing. Constants cost nothing against that budget.
// To change a set, edit the lines below and re-save.
//
// The active set is chosen from the CHART's market, which is legal because
// request.security only needs a `simple string` and syminfo.prefix is simple.
// Result: 32 symbols PER MARKET on the same 40-request budget, and every row
// shares the chart's own bar boundary — which removes the one-bar cross-exchange
// offset at source instead of tolerating it.

s1 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:TCS" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:BTCUSDT" : "NASDAQ:AAPL"
s2 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:INFY" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ETHUSDT" : "NASDAQ:MSFT"
s3 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:RELIANCE" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:SOLUSDT" : "NASDAQ:NVDA"
s4 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:HDFCBANK" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:BNBUSDT" : "NASDAQ:GOOGL"
s5 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:ICICIBANK" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:XRPUSDT" : "NASDAQ:AMZN"
s6 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:ITC" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ADAUSDT" : "NASDAQ:META"
s7 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:LT" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:DOGEUSDT" : "NASDAQ:TSLA"
s8 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:SBIN" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:AVAXUSDT" : "NASDAQ:AVGO"
s9 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:BHARTIARTL" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:LINKUSDT" : "NASDAQ:NFLX"
s10 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:ASIANPAINT" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:DOTUSDT" : "NASDAQ:AMD"
s11 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:MARUTI" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:LTCUSDT" : "NASDAQ:COST"
s12 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:AXISBANK" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:TRXUSDT" : "NASDAQ:ORCL"
s13 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:KOTAKBANK" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ATOMUSDT" : "NASDAQ:PLTR"
s14 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:BAJFINANCE" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:UNIUSDT" : "NASDAQ:CRWD"
s15 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:HINDUNILVR" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:NEARUSDT" : "NASDAQ:COIN"
s16 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:TITAN" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:APTUSDT" : "NASDAQ:MU"
s17 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:SUNPHARMA" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ARBUSDT" : "NYSE:BRK.B"
s18 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:WIPRO" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:OPUSDT" : "NYSE:JPM"
s19 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:HCLTECH" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:INJUSDT" : "NYSE:V"
s20 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:TECHM" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:SUIUSDT" : "NYSE:UNH"
s21 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:ADANIPORTS" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:TIAUSDT" : "NYSE:XOM"
s22 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:ONGC" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:SEIUSDT" : "NYSE:LLY"
s23 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:NTPC" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:FILUSDT" : "NYSE:CRM"
s24 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:POWERGRID" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:AAVEUSDT" : "NYSE:SAP"
s25 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:COALINDIA" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:MKRUSDT" : "NASDAQ:QQQ"
s26 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:TATAMOTORS" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ETCUSDT" : "AMEX:SPY"
s27 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:TATASTEEL" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:BCHUSDT" : "AMEX:VOO"
s28 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:NIFTYBEES" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:XLMUSDT" : "AMEX:IWM"
s29 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:JUNIORBEES" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:HBARUSDT" : "AMEX:XLK"
s30 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:MID150BEES" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ICPUSDT" : "AMEX:GLD"
s31 = chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:GOLDBEES" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:ALGOUSDT" : "NASDAQ:INTC"
// Slot 32 carries the CHART's own symbol so anything you open is scanned, even
// if it is not in the market set. Duplicates are removed in the display loop.
s32 = addChartSym ? syminfo.tickerid : chartMkt == "IN" ? "NSE:CPSEETF" : chartMkt == "CRYPTO" ? "BINANCE:VETUSDT" : "NYSE:IBM"

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CORE ENGINE — baseline money line (1-close flip, no gates)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
tr_ = ta.tr(true)
atrV = ta.rma(tr_, atrLen)
hh = ta.highest(high, longLen)
ll = ta.lowest(low, shortLen)
lsB = hh - atrMultL * atrV
ssB = ll + atrMultS * atrV

var float longStop = na
var float shortStop = na
longStop  := close[1] > nz(longStop[1], lsB) ? math.max(lsB, nz(longStop[1], lsB)) : lsB
shortStop := close[1] < nz(shortStop[1], ssB) ? math.min(ssB, nz(shortStop[1], ssB)) : ssB

var int trend = 1
// consecutive weekly closes on the wrong side of the line. With both confirms
// set to 1 this is mathematically identical to the original one-close rule.
var int belowN = 0
var int aboveN = 0
belowN := trend == 1 and close < longStop ? belowN + 1 : 0
aboveN := trend == -1 and close > shortStop ? aboveN + 1 : 0
trend := trend == -1 and aboveN >= entryConfirm ? 1 : trend == 1 and belowN >= exitConfirm ? -1 : trend
isFlip = trend != trend[1]
moneyLine = trend == 1 ? longStop : shortStop

buySignal  = isFlip and trend == 1
sellSignal = isFlip and trend == -1

var float entryPrice = na
var float exitPrice = na
// ── embedded track record (mini-backtest of this system on THIS symbol) ──
var int flipBarIdx = na
var int flipTime = na
var float lastFlipPx = na
var float flipClose = na
if isFlip
    flipTime := time
    flipBarIdx := bar_index
    lastFlipPx := moneyLine[1]   // the LEVEL that was crossed (the old tripwire), not the close
    flipClose  := close          // the PRICE when the regime turned, for the since-flip stat
var int tradeCount = 0
var int winCount = 0
var float grossWin = 0.0
var float grossLoss = 0.0
var float sysEquity = 1.0
var float firstEntry = na
var int firstEntryTime = na
var bool entryInBT = false
// whipsaw = sold, then bought back within `whipWeeks` bars at a HIGHER price
var int whipCount = 0
var float whipCost = 0.0
var float lastExitPx = na
var int lastExitBar = na
inBT = not btUseStart or year >= btStartY
if buySignal
    entryPrice := close
    entryInBT := inBT
    if inBT and na(firstEntry)
        firstEntry := close
        firstEntryTime := time
    if inBT and not na(lastExitPx) and not na(lastExitBar) and bar_index - lastExitBar <= whipWeeks and close > lastExitPx
        whipCount += 1
        whipCost += (close - lastExitPx) / lastExitPx * 100
if sellSignal
    exitPrice := close
    lastExitPx := close
    lastExitBar := bar_index
    if inBT and entryInBT and not na(entryPrice) and entryPrice > 0
        tradePnl = (close - entryPrice) / entryPrice * 100
        sysEquity := sysEquity * (1 + tradePnl / 100)
        tradeCount += 1
        if tradePnl > 0
            winCount += 1
            grossWin += tradePnl
        else
            grossLoss += -tradePnl

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// QUALITY CHECKS (grade, never gate)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Self-contained so the daily context recomputes the whole chain on DAILY bars
// rather than inheriting anything from the chart-timeframe `trend` variable.
f_trendOnly() =>
    _tr = ta.tr(true)
    _atr = ta.rma(_tr, atrLen)
    _hh = ta.highest(high, longLen)
    _ll = ta.lowest(low, shortLen)
    _lsB = _hh - atrMultL * _atr
    _ssB = _ll + atrMultS * _atr
    var float _ls = na
    var float _ss = na
    _ls := close[1] > nz(_ls[1], _lsB) ? math.max(_lsB, nz(_ls[1], _lsB)) : _lsB
    _ss := close[1] < nz(_ss[1], _ssB) ? math.min(_ssB, nz(_ss[1], _ssB)) : _ssB
    var int _t = 1
    var int _bn = 0
    var int _an = 0
    _bn := _t == 1 and close < _ls ? _bn + 1 : 0
    _an := _t == -1 and close > _ss ? _an + 1 : 0
    _t := _t == -1 and _an >= entryConfirm ? 1 : _t == 1 and _bn >= exitConfirm ? -1 : _t
    _t

dailyTrend = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_trendOnly(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
// The flip rule is timeframe-agnostic, so read it on all three at once.
// Chart TF then becomes a viewing choice, not a different system.
// NOTE ON REQUEST BUDGET: TradingView allows a maximum of 40 request.*() calls
// per script. This script uses 32 (focus list) + 1 (daily) + 1 (weekly) + 6
// (financials) = 40. It is FULL. Adding even one more request.security or
// request.financial call will break the entire indicator — it will compile-fail
// and draw nothing at all, not just lose the new feature. If you want another
// timeframe or symbol, you must remove an existing call first.
regD = dailyTrend
regW = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", f_trendOnly(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
// bars that equal N trading days on the chart timeframe (intraday falls back to N bars)
f_daysToBars(_d) =>
    timeframe.ismonthly ? math.max(2, math.round(_d / 21.0 / timeframe.multiplier)) : timeframe.isweekly ? math.max(2, math.round(_d / 5.0 / timeframe.multiplier)) : timeframe.isdaily ? math.max(2, math.round(_d / timeframe.multiplier)) : _d
ma50  = ta.sma(close, f_daysToBars(50))
ma100 = ta.sma(close, f_daysToBars(100))
ma200 = ta.sma(close, f_daysToBars(200))
rsiV = ta.rsi(close, 14)
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, 20)
volLive  = barstate.islast and time_close > timenow   // forming bar: its volume is partial, use the last finished bar
volRatio = volAvg > 0 ? (volLive ? volume[1] / volAvg[1] : volume / volAvg) : na
ext200 = ma200 > 0 ? (close - ma200) / ma200 * 100 : na

// first loaded bar's timestamp. `time[bar_index]` looks equivalent but Pine
// sizes its history buffer from CONSTANT offsets at compile time, so a dynamic
// offset silently returns na — which disables any check built on it.
var int firstBarTime = na
if na(firstBarTime)
    firstBarTime := time

// ── the script now describes whatever timeframe the chart is on ──
tfIntra = timeframe.isintraday ? (timeframe.multiplier >= 60 ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier / 60) + "h" : str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier) + "m") : ""
tfWord = timeframe.ismonthly ? (timeframe.multiplier > 1 ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier) + "-month" : "monthly") : timeframe.isweekly ? (timeframe.multiplier > 1 ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier) + "-week" : "weekly") : timeframe.isdaily ? (timeframe.multiplier > 1 ? str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier) + "-day" : "daily") : tfIntra
tfBar  = timeframe.ismonthly ? "mo" : timeframe.isweekly ? "w" : timeframe.isdaily ? "d" : tfIntra

coreName = str.tostring(ma200barLen) + (timeframe.isweekly ? "w" : timeframe.isdaily ? "d" : timeframe.ismonthly ? "mo" : "-bar")
// ── How old is this SYMBOL, in calendar terms? Bar count lies: a 7-week-old
// stock has ~200 bars on 4H and ~8 on weekly, but it is seven weeks old
// either way. A trailing stop needs the stock to have LIVED through
// something, not merely to have produced rows of data.
histDays = na(firstBarTime) ? na : (time - firstBarTime) / 86400000
thinHist = not na(histDays) and histDays < minHistDays
histTag  = thinHist ? "   ⚠ ONLY " + str.tostring(histDays, "#") + "d OF LOADED HISTORY — signals unreliable (zoom out / use a higher TF)" : ""

// RAW structural facts (direction-neutral) — used by the LONG-TERM rows
above200 = na(ma200) ? false : close > ma200
bullStack = na(ma50) or na(ma100) or na(ma200) ? false : ma50 > ma100 and ma100 > ma200
bearStack = na(ma50) or na(ma100) or na(ma200) ? false : ma50 < ma100 and ma100 < ma200

// ── CONFIRMATION CHECKS — every one reads WITH the current trend ──────
// A score is "how well confirmed is the state we are in", not "how bullish
// is everything". So in a downtrend, below-the-200 and a bearish stack COUNT.
// Without this, "Bearish 8/9" would have meant a downtrend under attack,
// which is the opposite of what the words suggest.
dRedundant = timeframe.isdaily
c1 = dRedundant or na(dailyTrend) ? true : dailyTrend == trend                                    // lower TF agrees
c2 = trend == 1 ? above200 : not above200                   // right side of the 200
c3 = trend == 1 ? bullStack : bearStack                     // MA stack aligned
c4 = na(volRatio) ? true : volRatio >= 1.0                  // participation
c5 = na(rsiV) ? true : (trend == 1 ? rsiV < 70 : rsiV > 30) // not exhausted either way

// ── c6 TREND STRENGTH (ADX) ──────────────────────────────────────────
// The check that speaks to whipsaw. ADX does not say which way price is
// going, only whether it is going anywhere. Below ~20 the market is ranging,
// which is exactly where a trailing stop gets chopped up.
[diPlus, diMinus, adxV] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
c6 = na(adxV) ? true : adxV >= adxMin

// ── c7 MOMENTUM THRUST (MACD histogram) ──────────────────────────────
// RSI < 70 says the move is not stretched. It never says the move has force.
[macdL, macdS, macdH] = ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
c7 = na(macdH) ? true : (trend == 1 ? macdH > 0 : macdH < 0)

// ── c8 NOT OVER-EXTENDED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// ext200 was already computed and never used. Entering 40% above the mean
// is a different trade from entering 5% above it.
c8 = na(ext200) ? true : math.abs(ext200) <= extMax

// ── c9 WEEKLY AGREES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// regW is already fetched for the REGIME row, so this costs nothing. It is
// auto-passed when the chart is weekly or higher: there `trend` IS the weekly
// read, and scoring it against itself would be circular, not confirming.
wRedundant = timeframe.isweekly or timeframe.ismonthly
c9 = wRedundant or na(regW) ? true : regW == trend

score = (c1 and not dRedundant ? 1 : 0) + (c2 ? 1 : 0) + (c3 ? 1 : 0) + (c4 ? 1 : 0) + (c5 ? 1 : 0) + (c6 ? 1 : 0) + (c7 ? 1 : 0) + (c8 ? 1 : 0) + (c9 and not wRedundant ? 1 : 0)
nChk     = 9 - (dRedundant ? 1 : 0) - (wRedundant ? 1 : 0)   // only checks that carry information on this timeframe
scorePct = nChk > 0 ? score / nChk : 0.0
// A grade is a claim about evidence. On a symbol with too little history the
// score is arithmetic, not evidence, so it gets no letter.
grade = thinHist ? "?" : scorePct >= 0.88 ? "A" : scorePct >= 0.66 ? "B" : "C"

var string lastBuyGrade = na
if buySignal
    lastBuyGrade := grade

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLOT — line, fill, 200d, clean graded signals
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
lineColor = trend == 1 ? bullColor : bearColor
mlPlot = plot(moneyLine, "Money Line", color = lineColor, linewidth = lineWidth, style = plot.style_stepline)
srcPlot = plot(close, "Price (invisible)", display = display.none)
fill(srcPlot, mlPlot, color = showFill ? (trend == 1 ? color.new(bullColor, 90) : color.new(bearColor, 90)) : na)
// CHART SYNC MODE — the fix for "the candles are squashed into a corner".
// TradingView scales the axis to fit EVERYTHING the indicator draws, not just
// price. A 200-bar mean far under price, a flip level 30% away, or a steep PRO
// trendline projected right all pull the axis with them: on GOLD weekly that
// put the scale at 250-6,000 for a symbol trading at 4,194, so the candles
// occupied a fifth of the pane.
// ON = compute everything exactly as before, draw only what sits near price.
// Signals, scores and the Focus List are byte-identical either way - this
// changes what is DRAWN, never what is decided.
syncMode = input.bool(false, "Chart sync mode — hide MAs, S/R and PRO lines so the axis follows price", tooltip = "OFF (default) = unchanged; every line is drawn and the axis stretches to fit them all.\n\nON = the moving averages, the Auto S/R lines, the flip-level line and the projected PRO trendlines are not drawn, so TradingView scales the axis to the candles. Everything is still CALCULATED - the breakout engine still reads the PRO lines, the panel still reports them - they are simply not rendered.\n\nTurn this on when the candles look compressed into part of the pane.", group = "2. Display")
plot(show200 and not syncMode ? ma200 : na, "200-day MA", color = color.new(color.red, 35), linewidth = 2)
ma200bar = ta.sma(close, ma200barLen)
plot(show200bar and not syncMode ? ma200bar : na, "200-bar MA", color = color.new(color.black, 0), linewidth = 3)
ma50bar = ta.sma(close, ma50barLen)
plot(show50bar and not syncMode ? ma50bar : na, "50-bar MA", color = color.new(color.orange, 20), linewidth = 2)
ma100bar = ta.sma(close, ma100barLen)
plot(show100bar and not syncMode ? ma100bar : na, "100-bar MA", color = color.new(#2962ff, 20), linewidth = 2)

// ── CORE variant: buy the same first signal, then hold until a weekly close
// breaks the 200-week line. Runs from the SAME start date as the system and the
// buy&hold figures so the three numbers are directly comparable.
var float coreEq    = 1.0
var float coreEntry = na
var bool  coreOn    = false
if not coreOn and buySignal and inBT
    coreOn    := true
    coreEntry := close
if coreOn
    if not na(coreEntry) and not na(ma200bar) and close < ma200bar
        coreEq    := coreEq * (close / coreEntry)
        coreEntry := na
    else if na(coreEntry) and not na(ma200bar) and close > ma200bar
        coreEntry := close

// Labels instead of plotshape: size is selectable and only the last N are kept.
// Drawn on CLOSED bars only so a forming bar can never leave a stray label.
sigSz = sigSizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : sigSizeIn == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small
var array<label> sigLbls = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  sigVLines = array.new<line>()
if (buySignal or sellSignal) and barstate.isconfirmed
    sigTxt = regimeMode ? (buySignal ? "bullish" : "bearish") : (buySignal ? "▲ BUY" : "▼ SELL")
    sigCol = regimeMode ? color.new(buySignal ? bullColor : bearColor, 15) : (buySignal ? color.new(#00c853, 0) : color.new(#d50000, 0))
    array.push(sigLbls, label.new(bar_index, buySignal ? low : high, sigTxt, style = buySignal ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = sigCol, textcolor = color.white, size = sigSz))
    if sigMax > 0 and array.size(sigLbls) > sigMax
        label.delete(array.shift(sigLbls))
    if showVL
        array.push(sigVLines, line.new(bar_index, low, bar_index, high + syminfo.mintick, extend = extend.both, color = buySignal ? color.new(#00c853, 40) : color.new(#d50000, 40), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
        if sigMax > 0 and array.size(sigVLines) > sigMax
            line.delete(array.shift(sigVLines))

// ── Flip Level line + label on chart (Bullmania-style) ──



showFlipLine = input.bool(true, "Show Flip Level Line + Label on Chart", group = "2. Display")
showScoreTag = input.bool(true, "Show CONFIRM score tag on chart", tooltip = "Small on-chart tag showing the n/N confirmation score for the CURRENT chart timeframe, next to the last bar.", group = "2. Display")
var line flipLn = na
var label flipLb = na
if barstate.islast and showFlipLine and not na(moneyLine)
    line.delete(flipLn)
    label.delete(flipLb)
    flipLn := line.new(bar_index - 10, moneyLine, bar_index + 8, moneyLine, extend = extend.right, color = color.new(color.yellow, 30), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
    flipLb := label.new(bar_index + 8, moneyLine, "Flip Level: " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 30), textcolor = color.yellow, size = size.small)

// on-chart confirm tag. Reads the CHART timeframe, same as the line it sits on.
var label scoreLb = na
if barstate.islast and showScoreTag
    label.delete(scoreLb)
    sTxt = thinHist ? "⚠ " + str.tostring(histDays, "#") + "d only" : (trend == 1 ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + str.tostring(score) + "/" + str.tostring(nChk) + ""
    sCol = thinHist ? color.new(#d50000, 15) : scorePct >= 0.88 ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : scorePct >= 0.66 ? color.new(color.orange, 20) : color.new(#d50000, 20)
    scoreLb := label.new(bar_index + 2, close, sTxt + "  ·  " + tfWord, style = label.style_label_left, color = sCol, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FUNDAMENTALS (real reported financials via request.financial)
// Stocks only — indices/crypto return na and the rows say "n/a"
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
showFund = input.bool(true, "Show Fundamentals Rows (stocks only)", group = "2. Display")
revTTM  = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "TOTAL_REVENUE", "TTM", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
revPrev = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "TOTAL_REVENUE", "FY", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
niTTM   = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "NET_INCOME", "TTM", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
roeFY   = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "RETURN_ON_EQUITY", "FY", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
deFY    = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "DEBT_TO_EQUITY", "FY", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
epsTTM  = request.financial(syminfo.tickerid, "EARNINGS_PER_SHARE_BASIC", "TTM", ignore_invalid_symbol = true)

netMargin = not na(revTTM) and revTTM > 0 and not na(niTTM) ? niTTM / revTTM * 100 : na
revGrowth = not na(revTTM) and not na(revPrev) and revPrev > 0 ? (revTTM - revPrev) / revPrev * 100 : na
peRatio   = not na(epsTTM) and epsTTM > 0 ? close / epsTTM : na

// hoisted: ta.* must run every bar (calling inside `if` blocks corrupts history)
hi52  = ta.highest(high, 52)
hiAll = ta.highest(high, 500)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// AUTO SUPPORT / RESISTANCE (swing pivots — where price reacted before)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
showSR   = input.bool(true, "Show Auto Support/Resistance Zones", group = "2. Display")
pivLen   = input.int(8, "S/R Pivot Strength (bars each side)", minval = 2, group = "2. Display")
srCount  = input.int(3, "How many levels each side", minval = 1, maxval = 6, group = "2. Display")


ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivLen, pivLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, pivLen, pivLen)

var array<float> resArr = array.new_float()
var array<float> supArr = array.new_float()
if not na(ph)
    array.unshift(resArr, ph)
    if array.size(resArr) > 40
        array.pop(resArr)
if not na(pl)
    array.unshift(supArr, pl)
    if array.size(supArr) > 40
        array.pop(supArr)

// nearest levels above / below current price
f_nearest(_arr, _above) =>
    float best1 = na, float best2 = na, float best3 = na
    if array.size(_arr) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(_arr) - 1
            v = array.get(_arr, i)
            ok = _above ? v > close : v < close
            if ok
                if na(best1) or (_above ? v < best1 : v > best1)
                    best3 := best2, best2 := best1, best1 := v
                else if na(best2) or (_above ? v < best2 : v > best2)
                    best3 := best2, best2 := v
                else if na(best3) or (_above ? v < best3 : v > best3)
                    best3 := v
    [best1, best2, best3]

[r1, r2, r3] = f_nearest(resArr, true)
[sup1, sup2, sup3] = f_nearest(supArr, false)

var line lnR1 = na, var line lnR2 = na, var line lnR3 = na
var line lnS1 = na, var line lnS2 = na, var line lnS3 = na
var label lbR1 = na, var label lbS1 = na

f_srLine(line _ln, float _price, color _col) =>
    line.delete(_ln)
    line _out = na
    if not na(_price)
        _out := line.new(bar_index - 60, _price, bar_index + 10, _price, extend = extend.right, color = _col, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
    _out

if barstate.islast and showSR
    lnR1 := f_srLine(lnR1, r1, color.new(#ff5252, 30))
    lnR2 := f_srLine(lnR2, srCount >= 2 ? r2 : na, color.new(#ff5252, 55))
    lnR3 := f_srLine(lnR3, srCount >= 3 ? r3 : na, color.new(#ff5252, 70))
    lnS1 := f_srLine(lnS1, sup1, color.new(#00e676, 30))
    lnS2 := f_srLine(lnS2, srCount >= 2 ? sup2 : na, color.new(#00e676, 55))
    lnS3 := f_srLine(lnS3, srCount >= 3 ? sup3 : na, color.new(#00e676, 70))
    label.delete(lbR1)
    label.delete(lbS1)
    if not na(r1)
        lbR1 := label.new(bar_index + 10, r1, "R " + str.tostring(r1, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(#ff5252, 40), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    if not na(sup1)
        lbS1 := label.new(bar_index + 10, sup1, "S " + str.tostring(sup1, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(#00e676, 40), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// AUTO TRENDLINES + RSI / MACD STATE
// Two lines through the last two swing highs / swing lows, extended right —
// the same wedge / channel you would draw by hand. A pivot needs `tlPiv` bars
// on each side to confirm, so a line re-anchors when a new swing confirms.
// The breakout marker fires on the bar that CLOSES through a falling
// resistance line (or below a rising support line).
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
showTL  = input.bool(true, "Show short-term trendlines + TL markers", tooltip = "Draws a line through the last two swing highs and the last two swing lows. Falling highs + a close above the line = breakout marker.", group = "2. Display")
tlPiv   = input.int(6, "Trendline pivot strength (bars each side)", minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = "2. Display")
tlColor = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 0), "Trendline colour", group = "2. Display")
showMom = input.bool(true, "Show MOMENTUM row (RSI + MACD state)", group = "2. Display")

tlPH = ta.pivothigh(high, tlPiv, tlPiv)
tlPL = ta.pivotlow(low, tlPiv, tlPiv)
var float hiA_px = na
var int   hiA_bar = na
var float hiB_px = na
var int   hiB_bar = na
var float loA_px = na
var int   loA_bar = na
var float loB_px = na
var int   loB_bar = na
if not na(tlPH)
    hiA_px  := hiB_px
    hiA_bar := hiB_bar
    hiB_px  := tlPH
    hiB_bar := bar_index - tlPiv
if not na(tlPL)
    loA_px  := loB_px
    loA_bar := loB_bar
    loB_px  := tlPL
    loB_bar := bar_index - tlPiv

float tlUpNow = na
float tlLoNow = na
if not na(hiA_px) and not na(hiB_px) and not na(hiA_bar) and not na(hiB_bar) and hiB_bar > hiA_bar
    tlUpNow := hiB_px + (hiB_px - hiA_px) / (hiB_bar - hiA_bar) * (bar_index - hiB_bar)
if not na(loA_px) and not na(loB_px) and not na(loA_bar) and not na(loB_bar) and loB_bar > loA_bar
    tlLoNow := loB_px + (loB_px - loA_px) / (loB_bar - loA_bar) * (bar_index - loB_bar)

tlBreakUp = showTL and not na(tlUpNow) and not na(tlUpNow[1]) and hiB_px < hiA_px and close > tlUpNow and close[1] <= tlUpNow[1]
tlBreakDn = showTL and not na(tlLoNow) and not na(tlLoNow[1]) and loB_px > loA_px and close < tlLoNow and close[1] >= tlLoNow[1]
plotshape(tlBreakUp, "Trendline breakout", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar, color = tlColor, size = size.tiny, text = "TL", textcolor = tlColor)
plotshape(tlBreakDn, "Trendline breakdown", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.orange, 0), size = size.tiny, text = "TL", textcolor = color.new(color.orange, 0))
var array<line> tlVLines = array.new<line>()
if (tlBreakUp or tlBreakDn) and showTLV and barstate.isconfirmed
    array.push(tlVLines, line.new(bar_index, low, bar_index, high + syminfo.mintick, extend = extend.both, color = tlBreakUp ? color.new(#2962ff, 45) : color.new(color.orange, 45), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
    if array.size(tlVLines) > 10
        line.delete(array.shift(tlVLines))

var line tlUpLn = na
var line tlLoLn = na
if barstate.islast and showTL
    line.delete(tlUpLn)
    line.delete(tlLoLn)
    if not na(tlUpNow)
        tlUpLn := line.new(hiA_bar, hiA_px, hiB_bar, hiB_px, extend = extend.right, color = tlColor, width = 2)
    if not na(tlLoNow)
        tlLoLn := line.new(loA_bar, loA_px, loB_bar, loB_px, extend = extend.right, color = tlColor, width = 2)

// momentum events (hoisted: ta.* must run every bar)
macdXUp  = ta.crossover(macdL, macdS)
macdXDn  = ta.crossunder(macdL, macdS)
macdXAge = ta.barssince(macdXUp or macdXDn)
rsiXUp   = ta.crossover(rsiV, 50)
rsiXDn   = ta.crossunder(rsiV, 50)
rsiXAge  = ta.barssince(rsiXUp or rsiXDn)

f_age(_n) =>
    na(_n) ? "" : _n == 0 ? "this bar" : str.tostring(_n) + tfBar + " ago"

f_dir(_v) =>
    _v > 0 ? "▲" : _v < 0 ? "▼" : "·"

f_tl(_a, _b, _now, _isRes) =>
    na(_now) ? "—" : (_b < _a ? "falling " : "rising ") + (_isRes ? "resistance " : "support ") + str.tostring(_now, format.mintick) + (_isRes ? (close > _now ? " — price ABOVE it" : " — " + str.tostring((_now - close) / close * 100, "#.#") + "% overhead") : (close < _now ? " — price BELOW it" : " — " + str.tostring((close - _now) / close * 100, "#.#") + "% cushion"))

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PRO LINES — long trendlines, channel, key levels
// Reads price history directly (indicator max_bars_back = 2000) and runs once,
// on the last bar. One linear block, no helper functions, no buffers.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float  proResNow   = na
float  proSupNow   = na
float  proResSlope = na
float  proSupSlope = na
int    proResT = 0
int    proSupT = 0
float  proKR   = na
float  proKS   = na
int    proKRn  = 0
int    proKSn  = 0
string proDbg  = ""
int    proBrkUpAgo = na
int    proBrkDnAgo = na

var line  proResLn = na
var line  proSupLn = na
var line  proChLn  = na
var line  proKRLn  = na
var line  proKSLn  = na
var label proResLb = na
var label proSupLb = na
var label proKRLb  = na
var label proKSLb  = na
var line  proBrkUpLn = na
var line  proBrkDnLn = na
var label proBrkUpLb = na
var label proBrkDnLb = na

if barstate.islast
    line.delete(proResLn)
    line.delete(proSupLn)
    line.delete(proChLn)
    line.delete(proKRLn)
    line.delete(proKSLn)
    label.delete(proResLb)
    label.delete(proSupLb)
    label.delete(proKRLb)
    label.delete(proKSLb)
    line.delete(proBrkUpLn)
    line.delete(proBrkDnLn)
    label.delete(proBrkUpLb)
    label.delete(proBrkDnLb)
    if showPro
        pL = math.min(proLB, bar_index - proS - 2)
        if pL <= 2 * proS + 3
            proDbg := "need more history (" + str.tostring(bar_index + 1) + " bars loaded)"
        else
            // ── 1. major swings, newest first (offset = bars ago) ──
            hO = array.new_int()
            hP = array.new_float()
            lO = array.new_int()
            lP = array.new_float()
            for o = proS to pL
                vH = high[o]
                vL = low[o]
                isH = true
                isL = true
                for j = 1 to proS
                    if high[o + j] >= vH or high[o - j] > vH
                        isH := false
                    if low[o + j] <= vL or low[o - j] < vL
                        isL := false
                    if not isH and not isL
                        break
                if isH and array.size(hO) < 30
                    array.push(hO, o)
                    array.push(hP, vH)
                if isL and array.size(lO) < 30
                    array.push(lO, o)
                    array.push(lP, vL)

            // ── 2. best trendline through two swings, resistance (side 0) and support (side 1) ──
            tol = proTol / 100.0
            float rSc = -1.0
            float rPa = na
            float rPb = na
            int   rOa = na
            int   rOb = na
            int   rT  = 0
            float sSc = -1.0
            float sPa = na
            float sPb = na
            int   sOa = na
            int   sOb = na
            int   sT  = 0
            for side = 0 to 1
                isRes = side == 0
                arrO = isRes ? hO : lO
                arrP = isRes ? hP : lP
                cnt  = math.min(array.size(arrO), 14)
                float bSc = -1.0
                float bPa = na
                float bPb = na
                int   bOa = na
                int   bOb = na
                int   bT  = 0
                if cnt >= 2
                    for k = 1 to cnt - 1
                        for m = 0 to k - 1
                            oa = array.get(arrO, k)
                            ob = array.get(arrO, m)
                            pa = array.get(arrP, k)
                            pb = array.get(arrP, m)
                            if oa - ob >= proS and oa > proRecent + 2
                                slope = (pb - pa) / (oa - ob)
                                ok = true
                                for q = proRecent to oa
                                    lv = pa + slope * (oa - q)
                                    cl = close[q]
                                    if isRes ? cl > lv * (1 + tol) : cl < lv * (1 - tol)
                                        ok := false
                                        break
                                lvNow = pa + slope * oa
                                if ok and lvNow > 0
                                    tc = 2
                                    for z = 0 to cnt - 1
                                        if z != k and z != m
                                            oz = array.get(arrO, z)
                                            if oz < oa
                                                lvz = pa + slope * (oa - oz)
                                                if math.abs(array.get(arrP, z) - lvz) <= lvz * tol * 1.5
                                                    tc += 1
                                    sc = tc * 100000.0 + oa * 10.0 - ob * 0.001
                                    if sc > bSc
                                        bSc := sc
                                        bPa := pa
                                        bPb := pb
                                        bOa := oa
                                        bOb := ob
                                        bT  := tc
                if side == 0
                    rSc := bSc
                    rPa := bPa
                    rPb := bPb
                    rOa := bOa
                    rOb := bOb
                    rT  := bT
                else
                    sSc := bSc
                    sPa := bPa
                    sPb := bPb
                    sOa := bOa
                    sOb := bOb
                    sT  := bT

            if rSc > 0
                proResSlope := (rPb - rPa) / (rOa - rOb)
                proResNow   := rPa + proResSlope * rOa
                proResT     := rT
                proResLn := line.new(bar_index - rOa, rPa, bar_index - rOb, rPb, extend = extend.right, color = proColor, width = 2)
                proResLb := label.new(bar_index + 1, proResNow, (proResSlope < 0 ? "↘ resistance " : "↗ resistance ") + str.tostring(proResNow, format.mintick) + " · " + str.tostring(rT) + " touches", style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(proColor, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
            if sSc > 0
                proSupSlope := (sPb - sPa) / (sOa - sOb)
                proSupNow   := sPa + proSupSlope * sOa
                proSupT     := sT
                proSupLn := line.new(bar_index - sOa, sPa, bar_index - sOb, sPb, extend = extend.right, color = proColor, width = 2)
                proSupLb := label.new(bar_index + 1, proSupNow, (proSupSlope < 0 ? "↘ support " : "↗ support ") + str.tostring(proSupNow, format.mintick) + " · " + str.tostring(sT) + " touches", style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(proColor, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

            // ── 2b. exact bar where price last closed through each long line ──
            if showProV
                if rSc > 0
                    for q = 0 to proRecent - 1
                        lvq  = rPa + (rPb - rPa) / (rOa - rOb) * (rOa - q)
                        lvq1 = rPa + (rPb - rPa) / (rOa - rOb) * (rOa - q - 1)
                        if close[q] > lvq and close[q + 1] <= lvq1
                            proBrkUpAgo := q
                            proBrkUpLn := line.new(bar_index - q, low[q], bar_index - q, high[q] + syminfo.mintick, extend = extend.both, color = color.new(#00c853, 0), style = line.style_dashed, width = 2)
                            proBrkUpLb := label.new(bar_index - q, low[q], "▲ BREAKOUT — long resistance broken", style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(#00c853, 10), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                            break
                if sSc > 0
                    for q = 0 to proRecent - 1
                        lvq  = sPa + (sPb - sPa) / (sOa - sOb) * (sOa - q)
                        lvq1 = sPa + (sPb - sPa) / (sOa - sOb) * (sOa - q - 1)
                        if close[q] < lvq and close[q + 1] >= lvq1
                            proBrkDnAgo := q
                            proBrkDnLn := line.new(bar_index - q, low[q], bar_index - q, high[q] + syminfo.mintick, extend = extend.both, color = color.new(#d50000, 0), style = line.style_dashed, width = 2)
                            proBrkDnLb := label.new(bar_index - q, high[q], "▼ BREAKDOWN — long support broken", style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(#d50000, 10), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                            break

            // ── 3. parallel channel line off the trendline with more touches ──
            if showChan and (rSc > 0 or sSc > 0)
                if rSc > 0 and (sSc < 0 or rT >= sT)
                    float offR = 0.0
                    for q = 0 to rOa
                        offR := math.min(offR, low[q] - (rPa + proResSlope * (rOa - q)))
                    if -offR > close * 0.01
                        proChLn := line.new(bar_index - rOa, rPa + offR, bar_index - rOb, rPb + offR, extend = extend.right, color = proColor, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
                else
                    float offS = 0.0
                    for q = 0 to sOa
                        offS := math.max(offS, high[q] - (sPa + proSupSlope * (sOa - q)))
                    if offS > close * 0.01
                        proChLn := line.new(bar_index - sOa, sPa + offS, bar_index - sOb, sPb + offS, extend = extend.right, color = proColor, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)

            // ── 4. nearest key horizontal level above (side 0) and below (side 1) price ──
            if showKeyLv
                kO = array.copy(hO)
                kP = array.copy(hP)
                array.concat(kO, lO)
                array.concat(kP, lP)
                nK   = array.size(kP)
                ktol = tol * 1.5
                for side2 = 0 to 1
                    above = side2 == 0
                    float bLvl = na
                    int   bCnt = 0
                    int   bFo  = na
                    float bDist = 1000000000.0
                    float sLvl = na
                    int   sFo  = na
                    float sDist = 1000000000.0
                    if nK > 0
                        for a = 0 to nK - 1
                            lv0 = array.get(kP, a)
                            if (above and lv0 > close) or (not above and lv0 < close)
                                kc = 0
                                sm = 0.0
                                fo = array.get(kO, a)
                                for o2 = 0 to nK - 1
                                    ov = array.get(kP, o2)
                                    if math.abs(ov - lv0) <= lv0 * ktol
                                        kc += 1
                                        sm += ov
                                        fo := math.max(fo, array.get(kO, o2))
                                avg = sm / kc
                                dd  = math.abs(avg - close)
                                if kc >= 2 and dd < bDist
                                    bDist := dd
                                    bLvl  := avg
                                    bCnt  := kc
                                    bFo   := fo
                                if dd < sDist
                                    sDist := dd
                                    sLvl  := avg
                                    sFo   := fo
                    useB = not na(bLvl)
                    kLvl = useB ? bLvl : sLvl
                    kN   = useB ? bCnt : 1
                    kFo  = useB ? bFo : sFo
                    if not na(kLvl) and not na(kFo)
                        kTxt = (above ? "R " : "S ") + str.tostring(kLvl, format.mintick) + (kN >= 2 ? " (" + str.tostring(kN) + "x)" : "")
                        if above
                            proKR  := kLvl
                            proKRn := kN
                            proKRLn := line.new(bar_index - kFo, kLvl, bar_index, kLvl, extend = extend.right, color = proLvlColor, width = 2)
                            proKRLb := label.new(bar_index + 1, kLvl, kTxt, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(proLvlColor, 20), textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
                        else
                            proKS  := kLvl
                            proKSn := kN
                            proKSLn := line.new(bar_index - kFo, kLvl, bar_index, kLvl, extend = extend.right, color = proLvlColor, width = 2)
                            proKSLb := label.new(bar_index + 1, kLvl, kTxt, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(proLvlColor, 20), textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
            proDbg := "swings H" + str.tostring(array.size(hO)) + " L" + str.tostring(array.size(lO)) + (rSc > 0 ? ", res ok" : ", no valid res line") + (sSc > 0 ? ", sup ok" : ", no valid sup line")

proBreakUp = not na(proResNow) and not na(proResSlope) and close > proResNow and close[1] <= proResNow - proResSlope
proBreakDn = not na(proSupNow) and not na(proSupSlope) and close < proSupNow and close[1] >= proSupNow - proSupSlope

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TABLE — five plain-language rows
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════



f_arw(_v) => na(_v) ? "—" : _v == 1 ? "▲ bull" : "▼ bear"
f_pc(_v) => na(_v) ? "—" : (_v >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(_v, "#") + "%"

posMap = tablePos == "Middle Left" ? position.middle_left : tablePos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : tablePos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : tablePos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.bottom_right
txtSize = tableSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : tableSize == "Small" ? size.small : tableSize == "Large" ? size.large : size.normal
var table t = table.new(posMap, 2, 29, border_width = 2)

if barstate.islast
    table.clear(t, 0, 0, 1, 28)   // wipe stale cells so mode switches render cleanly

    // ── is this bar actually finished? a flip on a forming bar can un-happen ──
    // not barstate.isconfirmed stays true all weekend once the session has ended.
    // The honest test is whether the bar's close time has actually passed.
    unconf  = time_close > timenow
    hrsLeft = (time_close - timenow) / 3600000
    leftTxt = na(hrsLeft) or hrsLeft <= 0 ? "" : hrsLeft >= 24 ? str.tostring(math.floor(hrsLeft / 24), "#") + "d " + str.tostring(math.floor(hrsLeft % 24), "#") + "h left" : str.tostring(math.floor(hrsLeft), "#") + "h left"
    // ── how far is the exit, and what size does that allow? ──
    // math.abs() hid the direction. In a downtrend the line sits ABOVE price and
    // is a BUY TRIGGER, not a stop — there is no position, so there is nothing to
    // size. Reporting "5.1% to exit, 19.7% position" in green on a symbol the
    // script says to stay out of is an invitation in the wrong direction.
    inPos    = trend == 1
    stopDist = not inPos or na(moneyLine) or close <= 0 ? na : (close - moneyLine) / close * 100
    trigDist = inPos or na(moneyLine) or close <= 0 ? na : (moneyLine - close) / close * 100
    posSize  = na(stopDist) or stopDist <= 0 ? na : riskPct / stopDist * 100

    // Row 0 — ACTION
    // quality grade alone is not a size. A grade-A signal whose stop is 20% away
    // still risks 20% of the position, so the stop distance caps the size.
    sizeHint = thinHist ? "unrated — " + str.tostring(histDays, "#") + "d history" : na(posSize) ? (grade == "A" ? "full size" : grade == "B" ? "half size" : "small/skip") : str.tostring(math.min(posSize, 100), "#.#") + "% of account at " + str.tostring(riskPct, "#.#") + "% risk"
    // two independent warnings — neither may hide the other
    unconfTag = (unconf ? "   ⚠ UNCONFIRMED — " + leftTxt : "") + histTag
    actionTxt = regimeMode ? ((trend == 1 ? "BULLISH — above the flip line" : "BEARISH — below the flip line") + unconfTag) : sellSignal ? "SELL NOW" + unconfTag : buySignal ? "BUY NOW (" + grade + " — " + sizeHint + ")" + unconfTag : trend == 1 ? "HOLDING" + unconfTag : "STAY OUT" + unconfTag
    actionCol = sellSignal ? color.new(#d50000, 0) : buySignal ? color.new(#00c853, 0) : trend == 1 ? color.new(#00e676, 20) : color.new(#ff1744, 20)

    // Row 1 — the one price that matters (the flip level)
    lvlName = regimeMode ? "Flip Level" : trend == 1 ? "Flip Level (SELL if " + tfBar + " close under)" : "Flip Level (BUY if " + tfBar + " close over)"

    // Row 2 — position
    pnlPct = na(entryPrice) or entryPrice == 0 ? na : (close - entryPrice) / entryPrice * 100
    posTxt = trend == 1 and not na(entryPrice) ? "Bought " + str.tostring(entryPrice, format.mintick) + " (" + (pnlPct >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlPct, "#.#") + "%)" + (na(lastBuyGrade) ? "" : "  grade " + lastBuyGrade) : trend == 1 ? "In uptrend (pre-history)" : na(exitPrice) ? "No position" : "Sold " + str.tostring(exitPrice, format.mintick)

    // hoisted so compact mode can use them too
    openPnlMultC = trend == 1 and entryInBT and not na(entryPrice) and entryPrice > 0 ? close / entryPrice : 1.0
    sysRet = (sysEquity * openPnlMultC - 1) * 100
    bhRet = na(firstEntry) or firstEntry == 0 ? na : (close - firstEntry) / firstEntry * 100

    // core rows — always shown (compact and full)
    distPct = moneyLine > 0 ? (close - moneyLine) / moneyLine * 100 : na
    lvlVal2 = str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + "  (price " + (distPct >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(distPct, "#.#") + "% vs level)"
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, regimeMode ? "TREND" : "ACTION", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, actionTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = actionCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
    table.cell(t, 0, 1, lvlName, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
    table.cell(t, 1, 1, lvlVal2, text_color = color.yellow, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
    distTxt = "price " + (close >= moneyLine ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((close - moneyLine) / moneyLine * 100, "#.#") + "% vs the line"
    table.cell(t, 0, 2, regimeMode ? "Distance" : "Position", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
    table.cell(t, 1, 2, regimeMode ? distTxt : posTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

    // ═══ REGIME PANEL — the whole table collapses to state, nothing else ═══
    if regimeMode
        rgD = f_arw(regD)
        rgW = f_arw(regW)
        rgC = f_arw(trend)
        nBull = (regD == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (regW == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (trend == 1 ? 1 : 0)
        conflu = na(regD) or na(regW) ? "partial data" : nBull == 3 ? "ALIGNED BULL" : nBull == 0 ? "ALIGNED BEAR" : "CONFLICT (" + str.tostring(nBull) + "/3 bull)"
        confluCol = na(regD) or na(regW) ? color.new(color.gray, 55) : nBull == 3 ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : nBull == 0 ? color.new(#d50000, 20) : color.new(color.orange, 25)
        sfP = na(flipClose) or flipClose <= 0 ? na : (close - flipClose) / flipClose * 100
        sfB = na(flipBarIdx) ? na : bar_index - flipBarIdx
        rgRows = array.from("Confirm", trend == 1 ? "SELL trigger" : "BUY trigger", "Last Flip", "Flip Date", "Since Flip", "Risk to line", "Daily", "Weekly", "Chart (" + tfWord + ")", "Confluence")
        rgVals = array.from(
             thinHist ? "⚠ only " + str.tostring(histDays, "#") + "d of history" : (trend == 1 ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + str.tostring(score) + "/" + str.tostring(nChk) + " (" + (c1 ? "D" : "·") + (c2 ? "M" : "·") + (c3 ? "S" : "·") + (c4 ? "V" : "·") + (c5 ? "R" : "·") + (c6 ? "A" : "·") + (c7 ? "T" : "·") + (c8 ? "X" : "·") + (c9 ? "W" : "·") + ")",
             na(moneyLine) ? "—" : (trend == 1 ? "close below " : "close above ") + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick),
             na(lastFlipPx) ? "—" : str.tostring(lastFlipPx, format.mintick),
             na(flipBarIdx) ? "—" : str.format_time(flipTime, "yyyy-MM-dd"),
             na(sfP) ? "—" : (sfP >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sfP, "#.#") + "%  over " + str.tostring(sfB) + tfBar,
             not inPos ? (na(trigDist) ? "—" : "no position  |  buy trigger " + str.tostring(trigDist, "#.#") + "% above") : na(stopDist) ? "—" : str.tostring(stopDist, "#.#") + "% to exit  |  " + str.tostring(math.min(posSize, 100), "#.#") + "% position at " + str.tostring(riskPct, "#.#") + "% risk",
             rgD, rgW, rgC, conflu)
        for i = 0 to 9
            table.cell(t, 0, 3 + i, array.get(rgRows, i), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
            table.cell(t, 1, 3 + i, array.get(rgVals, i), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = i == 9 ? confluCol : i == 0 ? (thinHist ? color.new(#d50000, 15) : scorePct >= 0.88 ? color.new(#00c853, 25) : scorePct >= 0.66 ? color.new(color.orange, 25) : color.new(#d50000, 25)) : i == 5 ? (not inPos or na(stopDist) ? color.new(color.gray, 55) : stopDist <= 8 ? color.new(#00c853, 25) : stopDist <= 15 ? color.new(color.orange, 25) : color.new(#d50000, 20)) : color.new(color.gray, 55), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

    if not regimeMode and not compactMode
        // Row 3 — quality checks live
        qTxt = (trend == 1 ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + str.tostring(score) + "/" + str.tostring(nChk) + "   Daily " + (c1 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  200d " + (c2 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Stack " + (c3 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Vol " + (c4 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  RSI " + (c5 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  ADX " + (c6 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Mom " + (c7 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Ext " + (c8 ? "✓" : "✗") + (wRedundant ? "" : "  Wkly " + (c9 ? "✓" : "✗"))
        qCol = scorePct >= 0.88 ? color.new(#00c853, 40) : scorePct >= 0.66 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(#ff1744, 40)

        // Row 4 — LONG-TERM view in plain words
        ltTxt = above200 and bullStack and trend == 1 ? "HEALTHY UPTREND — ok to hold" :
             c2 and trend == 1 ? "UPTREND, early/rebuilding — hold with care" :
             not c2 and trend == 1 ? "RECOVERY ATTEMPT — not proven yet" :
             c2 ? "PULLBACK in uptrend — watch the line" :
             "DOWNTREND — do not hold long-term"
        ltCol = above200 and bullStack and trend == 1 ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : trend == 1 or above200 ? color.new(color.orange, 20) : color.new(#d50000, 20)

        table.cell(t, 0, 3, "Quality", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 3, qTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = qCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 0, 4, "MEDIUM-TERM (200d)", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 4, ltTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = ltCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Track Record + Asset Fit (the asset-map lesson, automated) ──
        pfVal = grossLoss > 0 ? grossWin / grossLoss : na
        winRate = tradeCount > 0 ? winCount / tradeCount * 100 : na
        // the record covers ALL loaded history, not just what is on screen —
        // show the start date so a 43/82 record is not mistaken for recent trades
        recStart = btUseStart ? "  |  from " + str.tostring(btStartY, "#") : na(firstEntry) ? "" : "  |  since " + str.format_time(firstEntryTime, "MMM yyyy")
        trTxt = tradeCount == 0 ? "no completed trades yet" : str.tostring(winCount) + "/" + str.tostring(tradeCount) + " wins  |  PF " + (na(pfVal) ? "∞" : str.tostring(pfVal, "#.##")) + recStart
        fitTxt = tradeCount < minTrades ? "COLLECTING DATA (need " + str.tostring(minTrades) + "+ trades)" : (not na(pfVal) and pfVal >= 1.5 and winRate >= minWin) or na(pfVal) ? "GOOD — system suits this asset" : pfVal >= 1.0 ? "MIXED — trade small here" : "POOR — hold or skip this asset"
        fitCol = tradeCount < minTrades ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : (not na(pfVal) and pfVal >= 1.5 and winRate >= minWin) or na(pfVal) ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : pfVal >= 1.0 ? color.new(color.orange, 20) : color.new(#d50000, 20)
        table.cell(t, 0, 5, "Track Record", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 5, trTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 60), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 0, 6, "ASSET FIT", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 6, fitTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = fitCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Early Entry scout: daily flipped up while weekly still bearish ──
        earlyTxt = trend == 1 ? "—  (already in: " + tfWord + " confirmed)" : dailyTrend == 1 and scorePct <= scoutPct ? "DAILY TURNED UP — scout entry possible (half size), full size on " + tfWord + " BUY" : dailyTrend == 1 ? "daily up, but the downtrend is still well confirmed — wait" : "no — daily still down, nothing to do"
        earlyCol = trend == 1 ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : dailyTrend == 1 and scorePct <= scoutPct ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : dailyTrend == 1 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(color.gray, 60)
        table.cell(t, 0, 7, "EARLY ENTRY", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 7, earlyTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = earlyCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Confirmation depth: consecutive weekly closes since the flip ──
        confN = na(flipBarIdx) ? 0 : math.min(bar_index - flipBarIdx + 1, 2)
        confTxt2 = trend == 1 ? (confN >= 2 ? "Bullish 2/2 — reinforced (2+ " + tfWord + " closes held)" : "Bullish 1/2 — fresh flip, could still fake out") : (confN >= 2 ? "Bearish 2/2 — reinforced" : "Bearish 1/2 — fresh flip")
        confCol2 = trend == 1 ? (confN >= 2 ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : color.new(color.orange, 25)) : (confN >= 2 ? color.new(#d50000, 20) : color.new(color.orange, 25))
        table.cell(t, 0, 8, "CONFIRM", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 8, confTxt2, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = confCol2, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── HOLD vs TRADE: system's compounded return vs buy&hold since first signal ──
        coreOpenMult = na(coreEntry) or coreEntry <= 0 ? 1.0 : close / coreEntry
        coreRet = coreOn ? (coreEq * coreOpenMult - 1) * 100 : na
        hvtNums = "   [ signals " + f_pc(sysRet) + "  ·  core/" + coreName + " " + f_pc(coreRet) + "  ·  hold " + f_pc(bhRet) + " ]"
        hvtTxt = na(bhRet) or tradeCount < minTrades ? "COLLECTING DATA (need " + str.tostring(minTrades) + "+ trades)" : (bhRet > sysRet * 1.3 and bhRet > 0 ? "HOLD — buy&hold beat the system here (compounder)" : sysRet > bhRet ? "TRADE — system beat buy&hold here" : "EITHER — similar results, your choice") + hvtNums
        hvtCol = na(bhRet) or tradeCount < minTrades ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : bhRet > sysRet * 1.3 and bhRet > 0 ? color.new(#2962ff, 20) : sysRet > bhRet ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : color.new(color.orange, 25)
        table.cell(t, 0, 9, "HOLD vs TRADE", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.navy, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 9, hvtTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hvtCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Last Flip: price + date (Bullmania-style) ──
        lfTxt = na(lastFlipPx) or na(flipBarIdx) ? "—" : "level " + str.tostring(lastFlipPx, format.mintick) + " crossed on " + str.format_time(flipTime, "yyyy-MM-dd")
        table.cell(t, 0, 10, "Last Flip", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 10, lfTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 60), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Tripwire: intraweek price vs the buy level (only meaningful while flat) ──
        twTxt = trend == 1 ? (buySignal and unconf ? "⚡ LIVE CROSS above the buy level — unconfirmed until the " + tfBar + " closes" : "—  (in position; watching exit level instead)") : close > moneyLine ? "⚡ PRICE ABOVE BUY LEVEL — unconfirmed until wk close (early-entry zone)" : "below buy level — waiting  (" + str.tostring((close - moneyLine) / moneyLine * 100, "#.#") + "% away)"
        twCol = trend == 1 ? (buySignal and unconf ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : color.new(color.gray, 60)) : close > moneyLine ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : color.new(color.gray, 50)
        table.cell(t, 0, 11, "TRIPWIRE", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 11, twTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = twCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Trend Stage: where price sits vs its own highs, and how mature the move is ──
        offHi = hi52 > 0 ? (close - hi52) / hi52 * 100 : na
        weeksIn = na(flipBarIdx) ? na : bar_index - flipBarIdx
        atNewHigh = close >= hiAll * 0.995
        stageTxt = trend != 1 ? "—  (no active uptrend)" : atNewHigh ? "BREAKOUT — at/near 500-bar highs, " + str.tostring(weeksIn) + tfBar + " into trend" : offHi > -3 ? "TESTING HIGHS — within 3% of 52-bar high, " + str.tostring(weeksIn) + tfBar + " in" : offHi > -15 ? "RECOVERING — " + str.tostring(-offHi, "#.#") + "% below 52-bar high, " + str.tostring(weeksIn) + tfBar + " in" : "EARLY — still " + str.tostring(-offHi, "#.#") + "% below 52-bar high, " + str.tostring(weeksIn) + tfBar + " in"
        stageCol = trend != 1 ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : atNewHigh ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : offHi > -3 ? color.new(color.orange, 25) : color.new(color.blue, 30)
        table.cell(t, 0, 12, "TREND STAGE", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.maroon, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 12, stageTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = stageCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Downside Context: how deep/stretched the decline is (descriptive, NOT a bottom call) ──
        ddPct = hi52 > 0 ? (close - hi52) / hi52 * 100 : na
        vs200w = ma200bar > 0 ? (close - ma200bar) / ma200bar * 100 : na
        rsiCold = not na(rsiV) and rsiV <= 35
        downTxt = trend == 1 ? "—  (in uptrend)" : not na(vs200w) and vs200w <= 2 and vs200w >= -8 ? "AT " + coreName + " LINE — historic cycle-low zone (" + str.tostring(ddPct, "#.#") + "% off high)" : not na(vs200w) and vs200w < -8 ? "BELOW " + coreName + " LINE — deep bear territory (" + str.tostring(ddPct, "#.#") + "% off high)" : rsiCold ? "STRETCHED — RSI " + str.tostring(rsiV, "#") + ", " + str.tostring(ddPct, "#.#") + "% off high, still above " + coreName + "" : "DECLINING — " + str.tostring(ddPct, "#.#") + "% off high, no exhaustion signs yet"
        downCol = trend == 1 ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : not na(vs200w) and vs200w <= 2 and vs200w >= -8 ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : rsiCold ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(color.gray, 45)
        table.cell(t, 0, 13, "DOWNSIDE CONTEXT", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.maroon, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 13, downTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = downCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── WHAT TO DO: full plain-English instruction, always on screen ──
        wtdRegime = trend == 1 ? "State is BULLISH. Line sits at " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + ". It turns bearish only on a " + tfWord + " CLOSE below that. No order is implied — decide your own size and horizon." : "State is BEARISH. Line sits at " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + ". It turns bullish only on a " + tfWord + " CLOSE above that."
        wtdTxt = regimeMode ? wtdRegime : buySignal ? "ENTER now (" + sizeHint + "). Set your exit at " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + ". Do nothing else until a " + tfWord + " close breaks it." : sellSignal ? "EXIT now at market. Then wait — do not re-enter until a new BUY prints." : trend == 1 ? "HOLD. Do nothing. Only act if a " + tfWord + " candle CLOSES below " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + " — then sell." : trend == -1 and dailyTrend == 1 and scorePct <= scoutPct ? "OPTIONAL scout: buy HALF size now, complete on a " + tfWord + " close above " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + ". Cut it if the daily rolls back over." : "STAY OUT. Do nothing. Wait for a " + tfWord + " close above " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + " — that is your only entry trigger."
        wtdCol = buySignal ? color.new(#00c853, 0) : sellSignal ? color.new(#d50000, 0) : trend == 1 ? color.new(#00c853, 35) : color.new(color.gray, 40)
        table.cell(t, 0, 14, "WHAT TO DO", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 14, wtdTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = wtdCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── BUSINESS QUALITY + VALUATION (reported financials) ──
        if showFund
            bqTxt = na(netMargin) and na(roeFY) ? "n/a (no financials for this symbol)" : "Net margin " + (na(netMargin) ? "—" : str.tostring(netMargin, "#.#") + "%") + "  |  ROE " + (na(roeFY) ? "—" : str.tostring(roeFY, "#.#") + "%") + "  |  Rev growth " + (na(revGrowth) ? "—" : (revGrowth >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(revGrowth, "#.#") + "%") + "  |  D/E " + (na(deFY) ? "—" : str.tostring(deFY, "#.##"))
            bqCol = na(netMargin) ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : netMargin >= 15 and (na(revGrowth) or revGrowth > 0) ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : netMargin >= 8 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(#d50000, 30)
            table.cell(t, 0, 15, "BUSINESS QUALITY", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.green, 25), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
            table.cell(t, 1, 15, bqTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bqCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

            valTxt = na(peRatio) ? "n/a" : "P/E " + str.tostring(peRatio, "#.#") + (peRatio < 15 ? "  — historically cheap zone" : peRatio < 30 ? "  — moderate" : "  — rich; needs growth to justify")
            valCol = na(peRatio) ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : peRatio < 15 ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : peRatio < 30 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(#d50000, 30)
            table.cell(t, 0, 16, "VALUATION", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.green, 25), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
            table.cell(t, 1, 16, valTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = valCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── Nearest support / resistance from swing pivots ──
        srTxt = (na(sup1) ? "support —" : "support " + str.tostring(sup1, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring((sup1 - close) / close * 100, "#.#") + "%)") + "   |   " + (na(r1) ? "resistance —" : "resistance " + str.tostring(r1, format.mintick) + " (+" + str.tostring((r1 - close) / close * 100, "#.#") + "%)")
        // ── REGIME (MTF): same line, three timeframes ──
        // third column is the CHART's own state — costs no request, and means
        // switching the chart to monthly gives you the monthly read for free
        bullN = (regD == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (regW == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (trend == 1 ? 1 : 0)
        anyNa = na(regD) or na(regW)
        mtfTxt = "daily " + f_arw(regD) + "     weekly " + f_arw(regW) + "     " + tfWord + " " + f_arw(trend) + "     —  " + (anyNa ? "partial data" : bullN == 3 ? "ALIGNED BULL" : bullN == 0 ? "ALIGNED BEAR" : "CONFLICT (" + str.tostring(bullN) + "/3 bullish)")
        mtfCol = anyNa ? color.new(color.gray, 55) : bullN == 3 ? color.new(#00c853, 20) : bullN == 0 ? color.new(#d50000, 20) : color.new(color.orange, 25)
        table.cell(t, 0, 21, "REGIME (MTF)", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 21, mtfTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = mtfCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── TRIGGER: the price that changes the state, spelled out ──
        trgTxt = na(moneyLine) ? "—" : trend == 1 ? "SELL / exit on a " + tfWord + " close below " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + "   (turns BEARISH)" : "BUY / enter on a " + tfWord + " close above " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + "   (turns BULLISH)"
        trgCol = na(moneyLine) ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : trend == 1 ? color.new(#d50000, 35) : color.new(#00c853, 35)
        table.cell(t, 0, 23, trend == 1 ? "SELL TRIGGER" : "BUY TRIGGER", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 23, trgTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = trgCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── SINCE FLIP: how long this regime has run and what it has paid ──
        sfPct = na(flipClose) or flipClose <= 0 ? na : (close - flipClose) / flipClose * 100
        sfWks = na(flipBarIdx) ? na : bar_index - flipBarIdx
        sfTxt = na(sfPct) ? "no flip on record yet" : (trend == 1 ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH") + " for " + str.tostring(sfWks) + tfBar + "  |  " + (sfPct >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sfPct, "#.#") + "% since the flip at " + str.tostring(flipClose, format.mintick)
        sfCol = na(sfPct) ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : (trend == 1) == (sfPct >= 0) ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : color.new(color.orange, 30)
        table.cell(t, 0, 20, "SINCE FLIP", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 20, sfTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = sfCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── WHIPSAW: exits that bought back higher soon after ──
        whipPct = tradeCount > 0 ? whipCount / tradeCount * 100 : na
        whipTxt = tradeCount < minTrades ? "COLLECTING DATA" : whipCount == 0 ? "none — no exit was re-bought higher within " + str.tostring(whipWeeks) + tfBar : str.tostring(whipCount) + " of " + str.tostring(tradeCount) + " exits bought back higher within " + str.tostring(whipWeeks) + tfBar + "  |  cost " + str.tostring(whipCost, "#.#") + "% total. Raise 'closes needed to SELL' to cut these."
        whipCol = tradeCount < minTrades ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : na(whipPct) or whipPct < 10 ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : whipPct < 25 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(#d50000, 25)
        table.cell(t, 0, 19, "WHIPSAW", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.maroon, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 19, whipTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = whipCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        // ── CORE EXIT: the slow line you hold a compounder against ──
        core200 = ma200bar
        coreGap = not na(core200) and core200 > 0 ? (close - core200) / core200 * 100 : na
        coreTxt = na(core200) ? "n/a — needs " + str.tostring(ma200barLen) + " bars of history" : close > core200 ? "HOLD CORE — 200-bar line at " + str.tostring(core200, format.mintick) + " (price " + (coreGap >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(coreGap, "#.#") + "% above). Core exits ONLY on a " + tfWord + " close below it." : "CORE BROKEN — " + tfWord + " close is below the 200-bar line at " + str.tostring(core200, format.mintick) + ". This is the long-term exit, not a dip."
        coreCol = na(core200) ? color.new(color.gray, 60) : close > core200 ? color.new(#2962ff, 25) : color.new(#d50000, 20)
        table.cell(t, 0, 18, "CORE EXIT (" + coreName + ")", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.navy, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 18, coreTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = coreCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        riskTxt = not inPos ? (na(trigDist) ? "—" : "no position — buy trigger sits " + str.tostring(trigDist, "#.#") + "% ABOVE price. Size is only meaningful once a stop exists below entry.") : na(stopDist) ? "—" : "stop is " + str.tostring(stopDist, "#.#") + "% away  |  at " + str.tostring(riskPct, "#.#") + "% risk that is a " + str.tostring(math.min(posSize, 100), "#.#") + "% position" + (stopDist > 15 ? "  — WIDE stop, ATR is inflated; size down hard" : stopDist > 8 ? "  — moderate" : "  — tight")
        riskCol = not inPos or na(stopDist) ? color.new(color.gray, 55) : stopDist <= 8 ? color.new(#00c853, 25) : stopDist <= 15 ? color.new(color.orange, 25) : color.new(#d50000, 20)
        table.cell(t, 0, 22, "RISK & SIZE", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 22, riskTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = riskCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

        table.cell(t, 0, 17, "S/R LEVELS", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.olive, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 17, srTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 55), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

    if compactMode and not regimeMode
        // smart note: surfaces the single most relevant secondary fact
        noteTxt = buySignal ? "ENTER now (" + sizeHint + "); exit at " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) : sellSignal ? "EXIT now at market; wait for next BUY" : trend == 1 ? "HOLD — only sell if a " + tfWord + " close breaks " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) : trend == -1 and dailyTrend == 1 and scorePct <= scoutPct ? "optional scout: half size now, complete on " + tfWord + " close above " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) : "STAY OUT — wait for a " + tfWord + " close above " + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring((close - moneyLine) / moneyLine * 100, "#.#") + "% away)"
        noteCol = trend == -1 and (dailyTrend == 1 and scorePct <= scoutPct or close > moneyLine) ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : color.new(color.gray, 55)
        table.cell(t, 0, 3, thinHist ? "⚠ HISTORY" : "NOTE", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 3, noteTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = noteCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
        // compact: long-term verdict (hold-vs-trade + structural health in one line)
        cLtTxt = (na(bhRet) or tradeCount < minTrades ? "fit: collecting data" : bhRet > sysRet * 1.3 and bhRet > 0 ? "HOLD-type (compounder)" : sysRet > bhRet ? "TRADE-type (signals win here)" : "either") + "  |  " + (above200 and bullStack and trend == 1 ? "healthy uptrend" : above200 and trend == 1 ? "uptrend rebuilding" : trend == 1 ? "recovery unproven" : above200 ? "pullback in uptrend" : "downtrend")
        cLtCol = above200 and bullStack and trend == 1 ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : trend == 1 or above200 ? color.new(color.orange, 30) : color.new(#d50000, 30)
        // Confirm score — five quality checks, shown as n/5 like the trend row
        // it sits under. This does NOT decide bullish/bearish; the flip line
        // does that. It says how much agreement is behind the current state.
        cfTxt = thinHist ? "⚠ only " + str.tostring(histDays, "#") + "d of history — score not meaningful" : (trend == 1 ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + str.tostring(score) + "/" + str.tostring(nChk) + "   Daily " + (c1 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  200d " + (c2 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Stack " + (c3 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Vol " + (c4 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  RSI " + (c5 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  ADX " + (c6 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Mom " + (c7 ? "✓" : "✗") + "  Ext " + (c8 ? "✓" : "✗") + (wRedundant ? "" : "  Wkly " + (c9 ? "✓" : "✗"))
        cfCol = thinHist ? color.new(#d50000, 15) : scorePct >= 0.88 ? color.new(#00c853, 25) : scorePct >= 0.66 ? color.new(color.orange, 25) : color.new(#d50000, 25)
        table.cell(t, 0, 5, "CONFIRM", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 5, cfTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = cfCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
        cTrgTxt = na(moneyLine) ? "—" : (trend == 1 ? "SELL on a " + tfWord + " close below " : "BUY on a " + tfWord + " close above ") + str.tostring(moneyLine, format.mintick)
        table.cell(t, 0, 6, trend == 1 ? "SELL TRIGGER" : "BUY TRIGGER", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 6, cTrgTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = trend == 1 ? color.new(#d50000, 35) : color.new(#00c853, 35), text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 0, 4, "LONG-TERM", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, 4, cLtTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = cLtCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

// ── TRENDLINES + MOMENTUM rows (placed after whichever panel is active) ──
if barstate.islast
    tlRow  = regimeMode ? 13 : compactMode ? 7 : 24
    momRow = regimeMode ? 14 : compactMode ? 8 : 25
    tlsRow = regimeMode ? 16 : compactMode ? 10 : 27
    if showPro
        resTxt = na(proResNow) ? "res: none" : (proResSlope < 0 ? "↘ res " : "↗ res ") + str.tostring(proResNow, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(proResT) + "x) " + (close > proResNow ? "price ABOVE" : str.tostring((proResNow - close) / close * 100, "#.#") + "% away")
        supTxt = na(proSupNow) ? "sup: none" : (proSupSlope < 0 ? "↘ sup " : "↗ sup ") + str.tostring(proSupNow, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(proSupT) + "x) " + (close < proSupNow ? "price BELOW" : str.tostring((close - proSupNow) / close * 100, "#.#") + "% away")
        keyTxt = (na(proKR) ? "" : "   |   level R " + str.tostring(proKR, format.mintick)) + (na(proKS) ? "" : "   S " + str.tostring(proKS, format.mintick)) + (na(proResNow) or na(proSupNow) ? "   [" + proDbg + "]" : "")
        proCol = not na(proResNow) and close > proResNow ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : not na(proSupNow) and close < proSupNow ? color.new(#d50000, 15) : color.new(color.gray, 55)
        table.cell(t, 0, tlRow, "TRENDLINES", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 25), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, tlRow, resTxt + "   |   " + supTxt + keyTxt + (na(proBrkUpAgo) ? "" : "   ▲ BREAKOUT " + f_age(proBrkUpAgo)) + (na(proBrkDnAgo) ? "" : "   ▼ BREAKDOWN " + f_age(proBrkDnAgo)), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = proCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
    if showTL
        tlTxt = na(tlUpNow) and na(tlLoNow) ? "not enough swing points yet" : f_tl(hiA_px, hiB_px, tlUpNow, true) + "   |   " + f_tl(loA_px, loB_px, tlLoNow, false)
        tlTxt2 = tlTxt + (tlBreakUp ? "   ▲ BROKE OUT this bar" : tlBreakDn ? "   ▼ BROKE DOWN this bar" : "")
        tlCol = tlBreakUp ? color.new(#00c853, 15) : tlBreakDn ? color.new(#d50000, 15) : color.new(color.gray, 55)
        table.cell(t, 0, tlsRow, "SHORT-TERM LINES", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 25), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, tlsRow, tlTxt2, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = tlCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
    if showMom
        rsiZone = na(rsiV) ? "" : rsiV >= 70 ? "overbought" : rsiV >= 50 ? "above 50" : rsiV > 30 ? "below 50" : "oversold"
        rsiPart = na(rsiV) ? "RSI —" : "RSI " + str.tostring(rsiV, "#") + " (" + rsiZone + ")" + (na(rsiXAge) ? "" : ", crossed " + (rsiV >= 50 ? "up " : "down ") + "50 " + f_age(rsiXAge))
        macdPart = na(macdL) or na(macdS) ? "MACD —" : "MACD " + (macdL > macdS ? "above signal" : "below signal") + (macdL > 0 ? ", above zero" : ", below zero") + ", hist " + (macdH >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(math.round(macdH, 2)) + (na(macdXAge) ? "" : ", crossed " + (macdL > macdS ? "up " : "down ") + f_age(macdXAge))
        momN = (not na(rsiV) and rsiV >= 50 ? 1 : 0) + (not na(macdL) and not na(macdS) and macdL > macdS ? 1 : 0)
        momCol = momN == 2 ? color.new(#00c853, 30) : momN == 0 ? color.new(#d50000, 30) : color.new(color.orange, 30)
        table.cell(t, 0, momRow, "MOMENTUM", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.purple, 20), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
        table.cell(t, 1, momRow, rsiPart + "   |   " + macdPart, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = momCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)
    // ── OUTLOOK: five votes, each +1 / 0 / -1. State of the evidence, not a forecast. ──
    olRow  = regimeMode ? 15 : compactMode ? 9 : 26
    trendF = trend == 1 ? 1 : -1
    mtfF   = na(regD) or na(regW) ? 0 : regD == regW ? (regD == 1 ? 1 : -1) : 0
    tlF    = showPro ? ((not na(proResNow) and close > proResNow) ? 1 : (not na(proSupNow) and close < proSupNow) ? -1 : 0) : not showTL ? 0 : (not na(tlUpNow) and close > tlUpNow) ? 1 : (not na(tlLoNow) and close < tlLoNow) ? -1 : 0
    rsiF   = na(rsiV) ? 0 : rsiV >= 50 ? 1 : -1
    macdF  = na(macdL) or na(macdS) ? 0 : macdL > macdS ? 1 : -1
    olN    = trendF + mtfF + tlF + rsiF + macdF
    olWord = olN >= 4 ? "STRONG BULLISH" : olN >= 2 ? "LEAN BULLISH" : olN <= -4 ? "STRONG BEARISH" : olN <= -2 ? "LEAN BEARISH" : "MIXED — no edge"
    olNote = not na(rsiV) and rsiV >= 70 ? "   |   RSI stretched — chasing risk" : not na(rsiV) and rsiV <= 30 ? "   |   RSI washed out — bounce risk" : ""
    olTxt  = thinHist ? "UNRATED — too little history" : olWord + "  (" + (olN > 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(olN) + " of 5)   line " + f_dir(trendF) + "  D+W " + f_dir(mtfF) + "  trendline " + f_dir(tlF) + "  RSI " + f_dir(rsiF) + "  MACD " + f_dir(macdF) + olNote
    olCol  = thinHist ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : olN >= 2 ? color.new(#00c853, 25) : olN <= -2 ? color.new(#d50000, 25) : color.new(color.orange, 30)
    table.cell(t, 0, olRow, "OUTLOOK", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = txtSize)
    table.cell(t, 1, olRow, olTxt, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = olCol, text_halign = text.align_center, text_size = txtSize)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SCANNER — same engine per symbol, bottom-right overview
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Everything below is evaluated in the REQUESTED symbol's own context, on its own
// bars. `_n` gives a deterministic warm-up guard, and returning the [1] values makes
// the reading independent of where each chart happens to sit inside its live bar.
f_scanTrend() =>
    _tr = ta.tr(true)
    _atr = ta.rma(_tr, atrLen)
    _hh = ta.highest(high, longLen)
    _ll = ta.lowest(low, shortLen)
    _lsB = _hh - atrMultL * _atr
    _ssB = _ll + atrMultS * _atr
    var float _ls = na
    var float _ss = na
    _ls := close[1] > nz(_ls[1], _lsB) ? math.max(_lsB, nz(_ls[1], _lsB)) : _lsB
    _ss := close[1] < nz(_ss[1], _ssB) ? math.min(_ssB, nz(_ss[1], _ssB)) : _ssB
    var int _t = 1
    var int _bn = 0
    var int _an = 0
    _bn := _t == 1 and close < _ls ? _bn + 1 : 0
    _an := _t == -1 and close > _ss ? _an + 1 : 0
    _t := _t == -1 and _an >= entryConfirm ? 1 : _t == 1 and _bn >= exitConfirm ? -1 : _t
    _lvl = _t == 1 ? _ls : _ss
    _dist = _lvl > 0 ? (close - _lvl) / _lvl * 100 : na
    _fresh = _t != _t[1]
    // warm-up guard: the trailing stop is path-dependent, so suppress output until
    // it has had enough bars to converge. Without this, a short-history symbol shows
    // a state that is really just an artefact of its seed value.
    var int _n = 0
    _n += 1
    _warm = _n > math.max(scanWarm, atrLen * 2)
    // read the last CLOSED bar of this symbol when confirmed mode is on
    // A bar is done when its close time has passed, regardless of whether a NEW
    // bar has opened yet. On a Saturday the week that ended Friday is finished,
    // but `[1]` would still point a week further back and `barstate.isconfirmed`
    // is still false — so both would read a full week stale exactly when you sit
    // down to review. `_done` reads the CURRENT bar once the session is over.
    _done = time_close <= timenow
    _off  = not scanConfirmed or _done ? 0 : 1
    _T  = _off == 0 ? _t : _t[1]
    _D  = _off == 0 ? _dist : _dist[1]
    _F  = _off == 0 ? _fresh : _fresh[1]
    _W  = _off == 0 ? _warm : _warm[1]
    _TM = _off == 0 ? time_close : time_close[1]
    // live bar disagrees with the confirmed bar = a flip is FORMING right now.
    // Packed into the same slot as `fresh` rather than adding a 5th tuple
    // element: each element of a request.security tuple counts against
    // TradingView's series budget, and 32 x 5 exceeds it. Bit 1 = confirmed
    // flip, bit 2 = live crossing.
    _P = _off == 1 and _W and _t != _t[1]
    // how long has this symbol been in its current regime?
    var int _fb = na
    if _t != _t[1]
        _fb := bar_index
    _bars0 = na(_fb) ? 0 : bar_index - _fb
    _BARS  = _off == 0 ? _bars0 : nz(_bars0[1], 0)
    // Slot packing: bits 1-2 are the two flags, everything above is the bar
    // count. A 5th tuple element blows TradingView's series budget (32 x 5),
    // so age rides along inside the flag instead of beside it.
    _FLAG = math.min(_BARS, 500) * 4 + (_W and _F ? 1 : 0) + (_P ? 2 : 0)
    [_W ? _T : na, _W ? _D : na, _FLAG, _TM]

[st1, sd1, sf1, sq1] = request.security(s1, scanTF, f_scanTrend(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true, currency = scanNoFx ? currency.NONE : syminfo.currency, calc_bars_count = scanBars)
[st2, sd2, sf2, sq2] = request.security(s2, scanTF, f_scanTrend(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true, currency = scanNoFx ? currency.NONE : syminfo.currency, calc_bars_count = scanBars)
[st3, sd3, sf3, sq3] = request.security(s3, scanTF, f_scanTrend(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true, currency = scanNoFx ? currency.NONE : syminfo.currency, calc_bars_count = scanBars)
